==Latvian==
{{slim-wikipedia|kivi (putni)|kivi (1)|lang=lv}}

===Etymology===
[[File:Tokoeka.jpg|250px|thumb|Kivi (1)]]
Via other European languages, ultimately borrowed from {{bor|lv|mi|kiwi}}, originally an [[onomatopoeic]] imitation of the bird's call. Originally the name of the bird, the English word [[kiwi]] soon became a term for people and things from [[New Zealand]], and was thus also used, initially as a brand name, for the fruit, which is also from [[New Zealand]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{lv-IPA|kivi}}
